    skos:prefLabel "4(3C) Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-4-2-ss-3c ;
    values:originalText "(3C) The court may require that a costs assessor certify that legal expenses have been properly incurred before permitting the payment of expenses from the disposal of any property covered by an order under subsection (3A) and may make any further or ancillary orders it considers appropriate. Refusal to make a restraining order" ;
