doc:sch-1-sec-45a-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "45A(2) Cessation of restraining orders relating to unexplained wealth" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) A *restraining order made under section 20A ceases to be in force if:  (a) an application for an *unexplained wealth order is made in relation to the *suspect to whom the restraining order relates; and  (b) the application is made within 28 days after the making of the restraining order; and  (c) the court refuses to make the unexplained wealth order; and  (d) one of the following applies: ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115  Schedule 1  Unexplained wealth" ;
    cof:pageNumber "11"^^xsd:integer .

concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-1-sec-8-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "8 Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-8-2 ;
    values:originalText "(i) the time for an appeal against the refusal has expired without an appeal being lodged;  (ii) an appeal against the refusal has lapsed;  (iii) an appeal against the refusal has been dismissed and finally disposed of.  (3) A *restraining order made under section 20A ceases to be in force if:  (a) an application for an *unexplained wealth order is made in relation to the *suspect to whom the restraining order relates; and  (b) the application is made within 28 days after the making of the restraining order; and  (c) the court makes the unexplained wealth order; and  (d) either:  (i) the unexplained wealth order is complied with; or  (ii) an appeal against the unexplained wealth order has been upheld and finally disposed of.  (4) If a *restraining order ceases under subsection (1) or (2), the court may, on application by a person with an *interest in the property covered by the restraining order, make any order as to costs it considers appropriate, including costs on an indemnity basis." ;
    skos:definition "(i) the time for an appeal against the refusal has expired without an appeal being lodged;  (ii) an appeal against the refusal has lapsed;  (iii) an appeal against the refusal has been dismissed and finally disposed of.  (3) A *restraining order made under section 20A ceases to be in force if:  (a) an application for an *unexplained wealth order is made in relation to the *suspect to whom the restraining order relates; and  (b) the application is made within 28 days after the making of the restraining order; and  (c) the court makes the unexplained wealth order; and  (d) either:  (i) the unexplained wealth order is complied with; or  (ii) an appeal against the unexplained wealth order has been upheld and finally disposed of.  (4) If a *restraining order ceases under subsection (1) or (2), the court may, on application by a person with an *interest in the property covered by the restraining order, make any order as to costs it considers appropriate, including costs on an indemnity basis."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "0b26c634e4cbbd7eff38f1d1a3e17dba3b59b98abe17bec6547f1d1bebe814c5" ;
    cof:pageNumber "12"^^xsd:integer ;
