    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-179c-ss-5 ;
    values:originalText "(5) The court may revoke the *preliminary unexplained wealth order on application under subsection (1) if satisfied that:  (a) there are no grounds on which to make the order at the time of considering the application to revoke the order; or  (b) it is in the public interest to do so; or  (c) it is otherwise in the interests of justice to do so." ;
    skos:definition "(5) The court may revoke the *preliminary unexplained wealth order on application under subsection (1) if satisfied that:  (a) there are no grounds on which to make the order at the time of considering the application to revoke the order; or  (b) it is in the public interest to do so; or  (c) it is otherwise in the interests of justice to do so."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "8103aec52462754b0f2cc78c2e0579169be59a0d36b2651f343a3a742443e6d0" ;
    values:partOf concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-1-sec-179c ;
    cof:pageNumber "14"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Court may revoke preliminary unexplained wealth order on application under subsection (1) if satisfied that there are no grounds, it is in the public interest, or it is otherwise in the interests of justice." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
