doc:sch-1-sec-179c-ss-5 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "179C(5) Application to revoke a preliminary unexplained wealth order" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(5) The court may revoke the *preliminary unexplained wealth order on application under subsection (1) if satisfied that:  (a) there are no grounds on which to make the order at the time of considering the application to revoke the order; or  (b) it is in the public interest to do so; or  (c) it is otherwise in the interests of justice to do so." ;
    cof:pageNumber "14"^^xsd:integer .

concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-1-sec-179ca a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "179CA Notice and procedure on application to revoke preliminary"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-179ca ;
    values:originalText "unexplained wealth order  (1) This section applies if a person applies under section 179C for revocation of a *preliminary unexplained wealth order.  (2) The applicant may appear and adduce material at the hearing of the application.  (3) The applicant must give the *DPP:  (a) written notice of the application; and  (b) a copy of any affidavit supporting the application. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115  Unexplained wealth  Schedule 1 Main amendments  Part 1  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010  (4) The *DPP may appear and adduce additional material at the hearing of the application.  (5) The *DPP must give the applicant a copy of any affidavit it proposes to rely on to contest the application.  (6) The notice and copies of affidavits must be given under subsections (3) and (5) within a reasonable time before the hearing of the application." ;
    skos:definition "unexplained wealth order  (1) This section applies if a person applies under section 179C for revocation of a *preliminary unexplained wealth order.  (2) The applicant may appear and adduce material at the hearing of the application.  (3) The applicant must give the *DPP:  (a) written notice of the application; and  (b) a copy of any affidavit supporting the application. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115  Unexplained wealth  Schedule 1 Main amendments  Part 1  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010  (4) The *DPP may appear and adduce additional material at the hearing of the application.  (5) The *DPP must give the applicant a copy of any affidavit it proposes to rely on to contest the application.  (6) The notice and copies of affidavits must be given under subsections (3) and (5) within a reasonable time before the hearing of the application."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "914109e940dc5287355cbb1b41a09cd9f8fc68e6676bd377724cb16612e7e0fb" ;
    cof:pageNumber "14"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-1-sec-179ca-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-1-sec-179ca-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-1-sec-179ca-ss-3 ;
