    values:originalText "reduced by any amount deducted under section 179J (reducing unexplained wealth amounts to take account of forfeiture, pecuniary penalties etc.).  (3) In proceedings under this section, the burden of proving that a person’s *wealth is not derived from one or more of the offences referred to in paragraph (1)(b) lies on the person.  (4) To avoid doubt, when considering whether to make an order under subsection (1), the court may have regard to information not included in the application.  (5) To avoid doubt, subsection (3) has effect despite section 317.  (6) Despite subsection (1), the court may refuse to make an order under that subsection if the court is satisfied that it is not in the public interest to make the order." ;
    skos:definition "reduced by any amount deducted under section 179J (reducing unexplained wealth amounts to take account of forfeiture, pecuniary penalties etc.).  (3) In proceedings under this section, the burden of proving that a person’s *wealth is not derived from one or more of the offences referred to in paragraph (1)(b) lies on the person.  (4) To avoid doubt, when considering whether to make an order under subsection (1), the court may have regard to information not included in the application.  (5) To avoid doubt, subsection (3) has effect despite section 317.  (6) Despite subsection (1), the court may refuse to make an order under that subsection if the court is satisfied that it is not in the public interest to make the order."@en ;
