doc:sch-1-sec-179h a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "179H Effect of property vesting in an insolvency trustee" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "In assessing the value of property of a person, property is taken to continue to be the *person’s property if it vests in any of the following:  (a) in relation to a bankruptcy—the trustee of the estate of the bankrupt;  (b) in relation to a composition or scheme of arrangement under Division 6 of Part IV of the Bankruptcy Act 1966—the trustee of the composition or scheme of arrangement;  (c) in relation to a personal insolvency agreement under Part X of the Bankruptcy Act 1966—the trustee of the agreement;  (d) in relation to the estate of a deceased person in respect of which an order has been made under Part XI of the Bankruptcy Act 1966—the trustee of the estate." ;
    cof:pageNumber "18"^^xsd:integer .

concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-1-sec-179j a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "179J Reducing unexplained wealth amounts to take account of"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-179j ;
    values:originalText "forfeiture, pecuniary penalties etc.  In determining the *unexplained wealth amount specified in an *unexplained wealth order in relation to a person, the court must deduct an amount equal to the following:  (a) the value, at the time of making the order, of any property of the person forfeited under:  (i) a *forfeiture order; or  (ii) an *interstate forfeiture order; or  (iii) a *foreign forfeiture order;  (b) the sum of any amounts payable by the person under:  (i) a *pecuniary penalty order; or  (ii) a *literary proceeds order; or  (iii) an order under section 243B of the Customs Act 1901; or  (iv) an *interstate pecuniary penalty order; or  (v) a *foreign pecuniary penalty order." ;
    skos:definition "forfeiture, pecuniary penalties etc.  In determining the *unexplained wealth amount specified in an *unexplained wealth order in relation to a person, the court must deduct an amount equal to the following:  (a) the value, at the time of making the order, of any property of the person forfeited under:  (i) a *forfeiture order; or  (ii) an *interstate forfeiture order; or  (iii) a *foreign forfeiture order;  (b) the sum of any amounts payable by the person under:  (i) a *pecuniary penalty order; or  (ii) a *literary proceeds order; or  (iii) an order under section 243B of the Customs Act 1901; or  (iv) an *interstate pecuniary penalty order; or  (v) a *foreign pecuniary penalty order."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "6e1194f6f13db0bfbbf2607dd2358cad10ab2cad4ed14b643570b0c2aa6570d5" ;
    cof:pageNumber "18"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Deduct unexplained wealth amounts from a person's total wealth when determining an unexplained wealth order." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf> ;
    dc:source "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.18" ;
