doc:sch-1-sec-179m a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "179M DPP may apply for an unexplained wealth order" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "The *DPP may apply for an *unexplained wealth order." ;
    cof:pageNumber "20"^^xsd:integer .

concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-1-sec-179n a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "179N Notice of application"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-179n ;
    values:originalText "(1) This section sets out the notice requirements if the *DPP has made an application for an *unexplained wealth order.  (2) If a court with *proceeds jurisdiction makes a *preliminary unexplained wealth order in relation to the person, the *DPP must, within 7 days of the making of the order:  (a) give written notice of the order to the person who would be subject to the *unexplained wealth order if it were made; and  (b) provide to the person a copy of the application for the unexplained wealth order, and the affidavit referred to in subsection 179B(2).  (3) The *DPP must also give a copy of any other affidavit supporting the application to the person who would be subject to the *unexplained wealth order if it were made.  (4) The copies must be given under subsection (3) within a reasonable time before the hearing in relation to whether the order is to be made." ;
    skos:definition "(1) This section sets out the notice requirements if the *DPP has made an application for an *unexplained wealth order.  (2) If a court with *proceeds jurisdiction makes a *preliminary unexplained wealth order in relation to the person, the *DPP must, within 7 days of the making of the order:  (a) give written notice of the order to the person who would be subject to the *unexplained wealth order if it were made; and  (b) provide to the person a copy of the application for the unexplained wealth order, and the affidavit referred to in subsection 179B(2).  (3) The *DPP must also give a copy of any other affidavit supporting the application to the person who would be subject to the *unexplained wealth order if it were made.  (4) The copies must be given under subsection (3) within a reasonable time before the hearing in relation to whether the order is to be made."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "c506acae73f3173882db5d2458a4accbbf8abb7b4bc55e760e8d1acf0ea49633" ;
    cof:pageNumber "20"^^xsd:integer ;
