doc:sch-1-sec-179p-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "179P(2) Additional application for an unexplained wealth order" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) The court must not give leave unless it is satisfied that:  (a) the *wealth to which the new application relates was identified only after the first application was determined; or ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115  Unexplained wealth  Schedule 1 Main amendments  Part 1  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010  (b) necessary evidence became available only after the first application was determined; or  (c) it is in the interests of justice to give the leave." ;
    cof:pageNumber "20"^^xsd:integer .

concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-1-sec-179q a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "179Q Procedure on application and other notice requirements"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-179q ;
    values:originalText "(1) The person who would be subject to an *unexplained wealth order if it were made may appear and adduce evidence at the hearing in relation to whether the order is to be made.  (2) The person must give the *DPP written notice of any grounds on which he or she proposes to contest the making of the order.  (3) The *DPP may appear and adduce evidence at the hearing in relation to whether an *unexplained wealth order is to be made." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The person who would be subject to an *unexplained wealth order if it were made may appear and adduce evidence at the hearing in relation to whether the order is to be made.  (2) The person must give the *DPP written notice of any grounds on which he or she proposes to contest the making of the order.  (3) The *DPP may appear and adduce evidence at the hearing in relation to whether an *unexplained wealth order is to be made."@en ;
