    cof:title "15F Unsigned freezing orders in court proceedings" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "If:  (a) it is material, in any proceedings, for a court to be satisfied that a *freezing order applied for under section 15D was duly made; and  (b) the form of freezing order signed by the magistrate is not produced in evidence; the court must assume that the order was not duly made unless the contrary is proved." ;
    cof:pageNumber "35"^^xsd:integer .

concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-2-sec-15g a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "15G Offence for making false statements in applications"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-15g ;
    values:originalText "A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person makes a statement (whether orally, in a document or in any other way); and  (b) the statement:  (i) is false or misleading; or ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115  Schedule 2  Other amendments relating to proceeds of crime" ;
    skos:definition "A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person makes a statement (whether orally, in a document or in any other way); and  (b) the statement:  (i) is false or misleading; or ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115  Schedule 2  Other amendments relating to proceeds of crime"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "8072385fe7fa0724a545c6f6d2dbc5d2f04925864eb70f4bfee6831fc069d589" ;
    cof:pageNumber "35"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Making false statements in applications is an offence." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
