doc:sch-2-sec-15h-ss-3 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "15H(3) Offences relating to orders made under section 15E" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(3) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person presents a document to a person; and  (b) the document purports to be a form of *freezing order under section 15E; and  (c) the document:  (i) has not been approved by a magistrate under that section; or  (ii) departs in a material particular from the terms given by the magistrate under that section. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115  Other amendments relating to proceeds of crime  Schedule 2 Freezing orders  Part 1  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010 Penalty: Imprisonment for 2 years or 120 penalty units, or both. Offence for giving form of order different from that served" ;
    cof:pageNumber "36"^^xsd:integer .

concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-2-sec-15h-ss-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "15H(4) Offences relating to orders made under section 15E"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-15h-ss-4 ;
    values:originalText "(4) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person gives a magistrate a form of *freezing order under section 15E relating to a *financial institution; and  (b) the person does so after presenting to the financial institution a document purporting to be a form of the freezing order; and  (c) the form given to the magistrate is not in the same form as the document presented to the financial institution. Penalty: Imprisonment for 2 years or 120 penalty units, or both." ;
    skos:definition "(4) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person gives a magistrate a form of *freezing order under section 15E relating to a *financial institution; and  (b) the person does so after presenting to the financial institution a document purporting to be a form of the freezing order; and  (c) the form given to the magistrate is not in the same form as the document presented to the financial institution. Penalty: Imprisonment for 2 years or 120 penalty units, or both."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "24f25abd1964b97f2cebd359cb2461327069b273d3a3afc643ca548691f184ef" ;
    values:partOf concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-2-sec-15h ;
    cof:pageNumber "36"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Giving a false document to a financial institution after obtaining a freezing order is an offence." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
