concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-2-sec-106 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "106 Subsection 42(5)"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-106 ;
    values:originalText "Repeal the subsection, substitute:  (5) The court may revoke the *restraining order if satisfied that:  (a) there are no grounds on which to make the order at the time of considering the application to revoke the order; or  (b) it is otherwise in the interests of justice to do so." ;
    skos:definition "Repeal the subsection, substitute:  (5) The court may revoke the *restraining order if satisfied that:  (a) there are no grounds on which to make the order at the time of considering the application to revoke the order; or  (b) it is otherwise in the interests of justice to do so."@en ;
