concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15g a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "15G Objects of Part"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-15g ;
    values:originalText "The main objects of this Part are:  (a) to provide for the authorisation, conduct and monitoring of controlled operations; and  (b) to exempt from criminal liability, and to indemnify from civil liability:  (i) law enforcement officers who, in the course of a controlled operation authorised under this Part, take an active part in, or are otherwise involved in, the commission of a Commonwealth offence or an offence against a law of a State or Territory or conduct that may result in a civil liability; and  (ii) certain other persons who, in accordance with the instructions of a law enforcement officer and in the course of a controlled operation authorised under this Part, take an active part in, or are otherwise involved in, the commission of a Commonwealth offence or an offence against a law of a State or Territory or conduct that may result in a civil liability." ;
    skos:definition "The main objects of this Part are:  (a) to provide for the authorisation, conduct and monitoring of controlled operations; and  (b) to exempt from criminal liability, and to indemnify from civil liability:  (i) law enforcement officers who, in the course of a controlled operation authorised under this Part, take an active part in, or are otherwise involved in, the commission of a Commonwealth offence or an offence against a law of a State or Territory or conduct that may result in a civil liability; and  (ii) certain other persons who, in accordance with the instructions of a law enforcement officer and in the course of a controlled operation authorised under this Part, take an active part in, or are otherwise involved in, the commission of a Commonwealth offence or an offence against a law of a State or Territory or conduct that may result in a civil liability."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "77b795c769cab3309be0a4a01dfeeb1a4cef938128620ab6e75fa033ec74689e" ;
    cof:pageNumber "62"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Exempts law enforcement officers and certain other persons from criminal liability and civil liability in the course of a controlled operation." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf> ;
    dc:source "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.62" ;
    cml:asserts concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15g-norm .
concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15g-norm a values:Obligation ;
    cml:modality cml:Deontic ;
    values:partOf concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15g ;
    values:borneBy values:State ;
    skos:scopeNote "borne by: State" ;
    values:deonticStatus values:HeuristicDerived ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed .
concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15g cml:asserts concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15g-logic-deontic-1 .
concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15g-logic-deontic-1 a cml:LogicApplication ;
    cml:modality cml:Deontic ;
    cml:operator "Exemption" ;
    cml:logicSummary "Exempts individuals from liability" ;
    cml:premiseText "Law enforcement officers and certain other persons are exempt from criminal liability and civil liability." ;
    cml:conclusionText "No liability for the individual." ;
    cml:executionSurface "modalities::logic::deontic" ;
    cml:confidence "1.0000"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed .

concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15g cml:asserts concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15g-logic-deontic-2 .
concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15g-logic-deontic-2 a cml:LogicApplication ;
    cml:modality cml:Deontic ;
    cml:operator "Permission" ;
    cml:logicSummary "Permits law enforcement officers and certain other persons to engage in activities without liability" ;
    cml:premiseText "The exemption permits law enforcement officers who take an active part in a controlled operation to engage in the commission of a Commonwealth offence or an offence against a law of a State or Territory." ;
    cml:conclusionText "Law enforcement officers are permitted to engage in the commission of a Commonwealth offence or an offence against a law of a State or Territory without liability." ;
    cml:executionSurface "modalities::logic::deontic" ;
    cml:confidence "1.0000"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed .

concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15g cml:asserts concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15g-logic-deontic-3 .
concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15g-logic-deontic-3 a cml:LogicApplication ;
    cml:modality cml:Deontic ;
    cml:operator "Obligation" ;
    cml:logicSummary "Imposes an obligation on law enforcement officers and certain other persons to take part in controlled operations" ;
    cml:premiseText "The exemption requires law enforcement officers who take an active part in a controlled operation to engage in the commission of a Commonwealth offence or an offence against a law of a State or Territory." ;
    cml:conclusionText "Law enforcement officers have an obligation to take part in controlled operations." ;
    cml:executionSurface "modalities::logic::deontic" ;
    cml:confidence "1.0000"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed .

concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15g cml:asserts concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15g-logic-deontic-4 .
concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15g-logic-deontic-4 a cml:LogicApplication ;
    cml:modality cml:Deontic ;
    cml:operator "Right" ;
    cml:logicSummary "Grants law enforcement officers and certain other persons the right to engage in activities without liability" ;
    cml:premiseText "The exemption grants law enforcement officers who take an active part in a controlled operation the right to engage in the commission of a Commonwealth offence or an offence against a law of a State or Territory." ;
    cml:conclusionText "Law enforcement officers have the right to engage in the commission of a Commonwealth offence or an offence against a law of a State or Territory without liability." ;
    cml:executionSurface "modalities::logic::deontic" ;
    cml:confidence "1.0000"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed .

concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15g cml:asserts concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15g-logic-deontic-5 .
concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15g-logic-deontic-5 a cml:LogicApplication ;
    cml:modality cml:Deontic ;
    cml:operator "Undertaking" ;
    cml:logicSummary "Establishes the scope and conditions of exemption" ;
    cml:premiseText "The exemption applies to law enforcement officers who take an active part in a controlled operation and certain other persons who follow instructions from a law enforcement officer." ;
    cml:conclusionText "The exemption is established for law enforcement officers and certain other persons under specific conditions." ;
    cml:executionSurface "modalities::logic::deontic" ;
    cml:confidence "1.0000"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed .
doc:sch-3-sec-15g a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "15G Objects of Part" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "The main objects of this Part are:  (a) to provide for the authorisation, conduct and monitoring of controlled operations; and  (b) to exempt from criminal liability, and to indemnify from civil liability:  (i) law enforcement officers who, in the course of a controlled operation authorised under this Part, take an active part in, or are otherwise involved in, the commission of a Commonwealth offence or an offence against a law of a State or Territory or conduct that may result in a civil liability; and  (ii) certain other persons who, in accordance with the instructions of a law enforcement officer and in the course of a controlled operation authorised under this Part, take an active part in, or are otherwise involved in, the commission of a Commonwealth offence or an offence against a law of a State or Territory or conduct that may result in a civil liability." ;
    cof:pageNumber "62"^^xsd:integer .

concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15ga a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "15GA Relationship to other laws and matters"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-15ga ;
    values:originalText "(1) Subject to subsection (2) and section 15HZ, this Part is not intended to limit a discretion that a court has:  (a) to admit or exclude evidence in any proceedings; or  (b) to stay criminal proceedings in the interests of justice.  (2) In determining whether evidence should be admitted or excluded in any proceedings, the fact that the evidence was obtained as a result of a person engaging in criminal activity is to be disregarded if:  (a) both: ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and witness identity protection  Schedule 3 Main amendments  Part 1  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010  (i) the person was a participant in a controlled operation authorised under this Part acting in the course of the controlled operation; and  (ii) the criminal activity was controlled conduct; or  (b) both:  (i) the person was a participant in an operation authorised under a corresponding State controlled operations law acting in the course of that operation; and  (ii) the criminal activity was conduct constituting an offence for which a person would, but for section 15HH, be criminally responsible." ;
    skos:definition "(1) Subject to subsection (2) and section 15HZ, this Part is not intended to limit a discretion that a court has:  (a) to admit or exclude evidence in any proceedings; or  (b) to stay criminal proceedings in the interests of justice.  (2) In determining whether evidence should be admitted or excluded in any proceedings, the fact that the evidence was obtained as a result of a person engaging in criminal activity is to be disregarded if:  (a) both: ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and witness identity protection  Schedule 3 Main amendments  Part 1  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010  (i) the person was a participant in a controlled operation authorised under this Part acting in the course of the controlled operation; and  (ii) the criminal activity was controlled conduct; or  (b) both:  (i) the person was a participant in an operation authorised under a corresponding State controlled operations law acting in the course of that operation; and  (ii) the criminal activity was conduct constituting an offence for which a person would, but for section 15HH, be criminally responsible."@en ;
