doc:sch-3-sec-15gd-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "15GD(2) Meaning of controlled operation and major controlled" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) A major controlled operation is a controlled operation that is likely to:  (a) involve the infiltration of an organised criminal group by one or more undercover law enforcement officers for a period of more than 7 days; or  (b) continue for more than 3 months; or  (c) be directed against suspected criminal activity that includes a threat to human life. Note: Section 15GN specifies when a controlled operation begins and ends." ;
    cof:pageNumber "66"^^xsd:integer .

concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15ge a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "15GE Meaning of serious Commonwealth offence and serious State"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-15ge ;
    values:originalText "offence that has a federal aspect Meaning of serious Commonwealth offence  (1) For the purposes of this Part, serious Commonwealth offence means a Commonwealth offence that:  (a) involves a matter mentioned in subsection (2); and  (b) is punishable on conviction by imprisonment for a period of 3 years or more.  (2) The matters are as follows:  (a) theft;  (b) fraud;  (c) tax evasion;  (d) currency violations;  (e) controlled substances;  (f) illegal gambling; ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115  Schedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and witness identity protection" ;
    skos:definition "offence that has a federal aspect Meaning of serious Commonwealth offence  (1) For the purposes of this Part, serious Commonwealth offence means a Commonwealth offence that:  (a) involves a matter mentioned in subsection (2); and  (b) is punishable on conviction by imprisonment for a period of 3 years or more.  (2) The matters are as follows:  (a) theft;  (b) fraud;  (c) tax evasion;  (d) currency violations;  (e) controlled substances;  (f) illegal gambling; ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115  Schedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and witness identity protection"@en ;
