doc:sch-3-sec-15gh-ss-4 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "15GH(4) Applications for authorities to conduct controlled operations" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(4) An application (whether formal or urgent) must:  (a) provide sufficient information to enable the authorising officer to decide whether or not to grant the application; and  (b) state whether or not the proposed controlled operation, or any other controlled operation with respect to the same criminal activity, has been the subject of an earlier application (whether formal or urgent) for an authority or variation of an authority and, if so, whether or not the authority was given or the variation granted; and  (c) state the proposed period of effect of the authority, which must not exceed:  (i) in the case of a formal application—3 months; and  (ii) in the case of an urgent application—7 days. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115  Schedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and witness identity protection" ;
    cof:pageNumber "71"^^xsd:integer .

concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-68 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "68 Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-68 ;
    values:originalText "(5) An authorising officer may require an applicant to provide such additional information concerning the proposed controlled operation as is necessary for the proper consideration of the application.  (6) As soon as practicable after making an urgent application that was not made in writing, the applicant must make a written record of the application and give a copy of it to the authorising officer to whom the application was made." ;
    skos:definition "(5) An authorising officer may require an applicant to provide such additional information concerning the proposed controlled operation as is necessary for the proper consideration of the application.  (6) As soon as practicable after making an urgent application that was not made in writing, the applicant must make a written record of the application and give a copy of it to the authorising officer to whom the application was made."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "ed3e7243be3ce02b96dff44acfb3efec4f4c0a517c5cf6b5b16cb357814f2a0e" ;
    cof:pageNumber "72"^^xsd:integer ;
