    skos:definition "(3) A person is sufficiently identified for the purposes of paragraph (1)(e) or (2)(e) if the person is identified:  (a) by an assumed name under which the person is operating; or  (b) by a code name or code number; as long as the chief officer of the authorising agency for the controlled operation can match the assumed name, code name or code number to the person’s identity."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "0be9a3baf7e4f1c1485320bdd3a44fc09bed89b8f1874c88bfe7ee0b26d141ae" ;
    values:partOf concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-72 ;
    cof:pageNumber "76"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "A person is sufficiently identified if they can be matched to their identity by the chief officer of the authorising agency." ;
