concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15go a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "15GO Variation of authority by appropriate authorising officer"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-15go ;
    values:originalText "(1) An appropriate authorising officer may vary an authority:  (a) at any time on the authorising officer’s own initiative; or  (b) on application under subsection 15GP(1).  (2) A variation may:  (a) extend the period of effect of the authority (subject to subsections (3) and (4)); or  (b) authorise additional persons to engage in controlled conduct for the purposes of the controlled operation and specify:  (i) with respect to additional law enforcement participants—the nature of the controlled conduct that those participants may engage in; and  (ii) with respect to additional civilian participants—the particular controlled conduct (if any) that each such participant may engage in; or  (c) provide that specified persons are no longer authorised to engage in controlled conduct for the purposes of the controlled operation; or  (d) authorise participants in the controlled operation to engage in additional or alternative controlled conduct.  (3) A variation cannot be made that has the effect of extending the period of effect of an urgent authority. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115  Schedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and witness identity protection" ;
    skos:definition "(1) An appropriate authorising officer may vary an authority:  (a) at any time on the authorising officer’s own initiative; or  (b) on application under subsection 15GP(1).  (2) A variation may:  (a) extend the period of effect of the authority (subject to subsections (3) and (4)); or  (b) authorise additional persons to engage in controlled conduct for the purposes of the controlled operation and specify:  (i) with respect to additional law enforcement participants—the nature of the controlled conduct that those participants may engage in; and  (ii) with respect to additional civilian participants—the particular controlled conduct (if any) that each such participant may engage in; or  (c) provide that specified persons are no longer authorised to engage in controlled conduct for the purposes of the controlled operation; or  (d) authorise participants in the controlled operation to engage in additional or alternative controlled conduct.  (3) A variation cannot be made that has the effect of extending the period of effect of an urgent authority. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115  Schedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and witness identity protection"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "363b6875d7f6a92d58faa95f0f7d792750eebc1ac73a4415aba791db4119a937" ;
    cof:pageNumber "77"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15go-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15go-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15go-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
