    values:originalText "(6) If the variation would extend the period of effect of a formal authority, the application (whether a formal variation application or an urgent variation application) must state the proposed period of the extension, which must not exceed:  (a) in the case of a formal variation application—the period that would result in the period of effect of the authority exceeding 3 months (including any previous extensions); and  (b) in the case of an urgent variation application—the lesser of:  (i) 7 days; and  (ii) a period that would result in the period of effect of the authority exceeding 3 months (including any previous extensions)." ;
    skos:definition "(6) If the variation would extend the period of effect of a formal authority, the application (whether a formal variation application or an urgent variation application) must state the proposed period of the extension, which must not exceed:  (a) in the case of a formal variation application—the period that would result in the period of effect of the authority exceeding 3 months (including any previous extensions); and  (b) in the case of an urgent variation application—the lesser of:  (i) 7 days; and  (ii) a period that would result in the period of effect of the authority exceeding 3 months (including any previous extensions)."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "c08a7a73272ab4a49a50fde42a2149238b76eb734a18039b71ef8fe19cfd1b5e" ;
    values:partOf concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15gp ;
    cof:pageNumber "78"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Application must state proposed period of extension not exceeding 3 months." ;
    dc:description "Proposed period of extension" ;
