concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15gq a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "15GQ Requirements for variation of authority"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-15gq ;
    values:originalText "(1) After considering an application for a variation of an authority, and any additional information provided under subsection 15GP(7), an appropriate authorising officer:  (a) may vary the authority in accordance with the application, either unconditionally or subject to conditions; or  (b) may refuse the application.  (2) An appropriate authorising officer must not vary an authority, whether on application or on the authorising officer’s own ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115  Schedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and witness identity protection" ;
    skos:definition "(1) After considering an application for a variation of an authority, and any additional information provided under subsection 15GP(7), an appropriate authorising officer:  (a) may vary the authority in accordance with the application, either unconditionally or subject to conditions; or  (b) may refuse the application.  (2) An appropriate authorising officer must not vary an authority, whether on application or on the authorising officer’s own ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115  Schedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and witness identity protection"@en ;
