concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15gs a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "15GS Form of variation of authority"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-15gs ;
    values:originalText "(1) A variation of an authority by an appropriate authorising officer (whether formal or urgent) must:  (a) identify the controlled operation to which the authority relates; and  (b) state the name and rank or position of the person varying the authority; and  (c) if the authority was varied on an application made under section 15GP, state:  (i) the name of the applicant; and  (ii) whether the application was a formal variation application or an urgent variation application; and ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115  Schedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and witness identity protection" ;
    skos:definition "(1) A variation of an authority by an appropriate authorising officer (whether formal or urgent) must:  (a) identify the controlled operation to which the authority relates; and  (b) state the name and rank or position of the person varying the authority; and  (c) if the authority was varied on an application made under section 15GP, state:  (i) the name of the applicant; and  (ii) whether the application was a formal variation application or an urgent variation application; and ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115  Schedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and witness identity protection"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "31ecf2967abd3705b0c1ad98be8d584581873ded8a91e02466214020b4b23463" ;
    cof:pageNumber "81"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Variation of authority must identify controlled operation, person varying authority, and application details." ;
    dc:description "Yes" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
