doc:sch-3-sec-15hb a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "15HB Indemnification of participants against civil liability" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "The Commonwealth must indemnify a participant in a controlled operation against any civil liability (including reasonable costs) the participant incurs because of conduct the participant engages in if: ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and witness identity protection  Schedule 3 Main amendments  Part 1  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010  (a) the participant engages in the conduct in the course of, and for the purposes of, the controlled operation in accordance with the authority to conduct the controlled operation; and  (b) the participant is identified in the authority as a person authorised to engage in controlled conduct for the purposes of the controlled operation; and  (c) the conduct does not involve the participant intentionally inducing a person to commit a Commonwealth offence or an offence under a law of a State or Territory that the person would not otherwise have intended to commit; and  (d) the conduct does not involve the participant engaging in any conduct that is likely to:  (i) cause the death of, or serious injury to, any person; or  (ii) involve the commission of a sexual offence against any person; and  (e) if the participant is a civilian participant in the operation—he or she acts in accordance with the instructions of a law enforcement officer; and  (f) the requirements (if any) specified in the regulations have been met." ;
    cof:pageNumber "88"^^xsd:integer .

concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15hc a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "15HC Effect of sections 15HA and 15HB on other laws relating to"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-15hc ;
    values:originalText "criminal investigation  Sections 15HA and 15HB do not apply to a person’s conduct that is, or could have been, authorised under Commonwealth law or a law of a State or Territory relating to the following:  (a) arrest or detention of individuals;  (b) searches of individuals;  (c) entry onto, or searches or inspection of, premises;  (d) searches, inspections or seizures of other property;  (e) forensic procedure;  (f) electronic surveillance devices or telecommunications interception;  (g) identification procedures;  (h) the acquisition or use of assumed identities;  (i) any other matter concerning powers of criminal investigation. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115  Schedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and witness identity protection" ;
    skos:definition "criminal investigation  Sections 15HA and 15HB do not apply to a person’s conduct that is, or could have been, authorised under Commonwealth law or a law of a State or Territory relating to the following:  (a) arrest or detention of individuals;  (b) searches of individuals;  (c) entry onto, or searches or inspection of, premises;  (d) searches, inspections or seizures of other property;  (e) forensic procedure;  (f) electronic surveillance devices or telecommunications interception;  (g) identification procedures;  (h) the acquisition or use of assumed identities;  (i) any other matter concerning powers of criminal investigation. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115  Schedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and witness identity protection"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "f403ef636f3396b1349cae92c3fa78283a5a4d017682fd87aaa3d372137c7d83" ;
    cof:pageNumber "89"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Exemptions from sections 15HA and 15HB" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
