doc:sch-3-sec-15hm-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "15HM(1) Chief officers’ 6 monthly reports to Ombudsman and" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) As soon as practicable after 30 June and 31 December in each year, the chief officer of each authorising agency must submit a report to the Ombudsman setting out the details required by subsection (2) in relation to controlled operations for which the agency was the authorising agency during the previous 6 months." ;
    cof:pageNumber "97"^^xsd:integer .

concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15hm-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "15HM(2) Chief officers’ 6 monthly reports to Ombudsman and"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-15hm-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) The report must include the following details:  (a) the number of formal authorities that were granted or varied by an authorising officer of the agency during the period to which the report relates;  (b) the number of formal applications for the grant of formal authorities that were refused by an authorising officer of the agency during the period to which the report relates, the date of those applications and the date of the refusals;  (c) the number of formal variation applications and urgent variation applications for the variation of formal authorities that were refused by an authorising officer of the agency during the period to which the report relates, the date of those applications and the date of the refusals;  (d) the number of urgent authorities that were granted or varied by an authorising officer of the agency during the period to which the report relates;  (e) the number of formal applications and urgent applications for the granting of urgent authorities that were refused by an authorising officer of the agency during the period to which the report relates, the date of those applications and the date of the refusals;  (f) the number of formal variation applications and urgent variation applications for the variation of urgent authorities that were refused by an authorising officer of the agency during the period to which the report relates, the date of those applications and the date of the refusals;  (g) the number of formal authorities that were varied by a nominated Tribunal member during the period to which the report relates;  (h) the number of formal variation applications and urgent variation applications for the variation of formal authorities that were refused by a nominated Tribunal member during ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115  Schedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and witness identity protection" ;
    skos:definition "(2) The report must include the following details:  (a) the number of formal authorities that were granted or varied by an authorising officer of the agency during the period to which the report relates;  (b) the number of formal applications for the grant of formal authorities that were refused by an authorising officer of the agency during the period to which the report relates, the date of those applications and the date of the refusals;  (c) the number of formal variation applications and urgent variation applications for the variation of formal authorities that were refused by an authorising officer of the agency during the period to which the report relates, the date of those applications and the date of the refusals;  (d) the number of urgent authorities that were granted or varied by an authorising officer of the agency during the period to which the report relates;  (e) the number of formal applications and urgent applications for the granting of urgent authorities that were refused by an authorising officer of the agency during the period to which the report relates, the date of those applications and the date of the refusals;  (f) the number of formal variation applications and urgent variation applications for the variation of urgent authorities that were refused by an authorising officer of the agency during the period to which the report relates, the date of those applications and the date of the refusals;  (g) the number of formal authorities that were varied by a nominated Tribunal member during the period to which the report relates;  (h) the number of formal variation applications and urgent variation applications for the variation of formal authorities that were refused by a nominated Tribunal member during ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115  Schedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and witness identity protection"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "34f934483783cfcde58bd34a2cca6e9be9ae22d15af12c04a1a2ee7e4868a97a" ;
    values:partOf concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15hm ;
    cof:pageNumber "97"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Report must include specific details about formal authorities and applications." ;
    dc:description "Yes" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
