doc:sch-3-sec-15hn-ss-7 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "15HN(7) Chief officers’ annual reports to Minister and Ombudsman" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(7) A copy of a report given to the Minister under this section must be given to the Ombudsman at the same time as it is given to the Minister." ;
    cof:pageNumber "100"^^xsd:integer .

concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15ho a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "15HO Annual report by Ombudsman"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-15ho ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Ombudsman must, as soon as practicable after 30 June in each year:  (a) prepare a report of the work and activities under this Part of the Ombudsman for the preceding 12 months and give a copy of the report to the Minister and to the chief officer of the law enforcement agency to which the report relates; and  (b) prepare a report of the work and activities of the Ombudsman for the preceding 12 months, being work or activities under a corresponding State controlled operations law, and give a copy of the report to the Minister and to the chief officer of the ACC.  (2) A report under this section must not include information which, if made public, could reasonably be expected to:  (a) endanger a person’s safety; or  (b) prejudice an investigation or prosecution; or ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115  Schedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and witness identity protection" ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Ombudsman must, as soon as practicable after 30 June in each year:  (a) prepare a report of the work and activities under this Part of the Ombudsman for the preceding 12 months and give a copy of the report to the Minister and to the chief officer of the law enforcement agency to which the report relates; and  (b) prepare a report of the work and activities of the Ombudsman for the preceding 12 months, being work or activities under a corresponding State controlled operations law, and give a copy of the report to the Minister and to the chief officer of the ACC.  (2) A report under this section must not include information which, if made public, could reasonably be expected to:  (a) endanger a person’s safety; or  (b) prejudice an investigation or prosecution; or ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115  Schedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and witness identity protection"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "05382ad6d12212c97ceca8ebf7e2ea6218a426ab7bf7cbcb87b948aa5facdf81" ;
    cof:pageNumber "101"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15ho-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15ho-ss-2 ;
