doc:sch-3-sec-106-ss-4 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "106(4) Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(4) The Ombudsman may receive from a State or Territory inspecting authority information relevant to the performance of the Ombudsman’s functions under this Division." ;
    cof:pageNumber "110"^^xsd:integer .

concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15hx a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "15HX Delegation by Ombudsman"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-15hx ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Ombudsman may, by written instrument, delegate to an APS employee responsible to the Ombudsman all or any of the Ombudsman’s powers under this Division, other than a power to report to the Minister.  (2) A delegate must, upon request by a person affected by the exercise of any power delegated to the delegate, produce the instrument of delegation, or a copy of the instrument, for inspection by the person." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Ombudsman may, by written instrument, delegate to an APS employee responsible to the Ombudsman all or any of the Ombudsman’s powers under this Division, other than a power to report to the Minister.  (2) A delegate must, upon request by a person affected by the exercise of any power delegated to the delegate, produce the instrument of delegation, or a copy of the instrument, for inspection by the person."@en ;
