concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15ka-ss-5 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "15KA(5) Application for authority to acquire or use assumed identity"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-15ka-ss-5 ;
    values:originalText "(5) An application:  (a) must be in writing in the form approved by the chief officer; and  (b) must contain:  (i) the name of the applicant; and  (ii) the name of the person to be authorised to acquire or use an assumed identity (if not the applicant); and  (iii) if the person referred to in subparagraph (ii) is not an officer of either an intelligence agency or a law enforcement agency or a foreign officer—the name and rank or position of the person proposed to be appointed as supervisor and an explanation of why it is necessary for a person who is not an officer to acquire or use the assumed identity; and  (iv) details of the proposed assumed identity; and  (v) reasons for the need to acquire or use an assumed identity; and  (vi) if the assumed identity is necessary for a purpose mentioned in subparagraph 15KB(2)(a)(i) or (ii)— details of the investigation or intelligence-gathering exercise in which the assumed identity will be used (to the extent known); and  (vii) details of any issuing agencies and the types of evidence to be issued by them; and  (viii) details of any application of a kind referred to in section 15KG (making entries in register of births, deaths or marriages) that is to be made under a corresponding assumed identity law. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115  Schedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and witness identity protection" ;
    skos:definition "(5) An application:  (a) must be in writing in the form approved by the chief officer; and  (b) must contain:  (i) the name of the applicant; and  (ii) the name of the person to be authorised to acquire or use an assumed identity (if not the applicant); and  (iii) if the person referred to in subparagraph (ii) is not an officer of either an intelligence agency or a law enforcement agency or a foreign officer—the name and rank or position of the person proposed to be appointed as supervisor and an explanation of why it is necessary for a person who is not an officer to acquire or use the assumed identity; and  (iv) details of the proposed assumed identity; and  (v) reasons for the need to acquire or use an assumed identity; and  (vi) if the assumed identity is necessary for a purpose mentioned in subparagraph 15KB(2)(a)(i) or (ii)— details of the investigation or intelligence-gathering exercise in which the assumed identity will be used (to the extent known); and  (vii) details of any issuing agencies and the types of evidence to be issued by them; and  (viii) details of any application of a kind referred to in section 15KG (making entries in register of births, deaths or marriages) that is to be made under a corresponding assumed identity law. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115  Schedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and witness identity protection"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "8aec59c5bf25d6785d452f1be4cae2a7e663fc462f66d6a93de35f8815124329" ;
    values:partOf concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15ka ;
    cof:pageNumber "116"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Application for authority to acquire or use assumed identity must be in writing and contain specific information." ;
    dc:description "yes" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
