concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15kc-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "15KC(2) Form of authority"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-15kc-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) An authority must state the following:  (a) the name of the person granting the authority;  (b) the date of the authority;  (c) details of the assumed identity authorised;  (d) details of any evidence of the assumed identity that may be acquired under the authority;  (e) the conditions (if any) to which the authority is subject;  (f) why the authority is granted;  (g) if the authority relates to an authorised intelligence officer, an authorised law enforcement officer or a foreign officer—the name of the officer;  (h) if the authority relates to an authorised civilian whose supervisor is a law enforcement officer:  (i) the name of the authorised civilian; and  (ii) the name of his or her supervisor under the authority; and  (iii) the period for which the authority will remain in force, being a period not exceeding 3 months;  (i) if the authority relates to an authorised civilian whose supervisor is an intelligence officer: ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and witness identity protection  Schedule 3 Main amendments  Part 1  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010  (i) the name of the authorised civilian; and  (ii) the name of his or her supervisor under the authority." ;
    skos:definition "(2) An authority must state the following:  (a) the name of the person granting the authority;  (b) the date of the authority;  (c) details of the assumed identity authorised;  (d) details of any evidence of the assumed identity that may be acquired under the authority;  (e) the conditions (if any) to which the authority is subject;  (f) why the authority is granted;  (g) if the authority relates to an authorised intelligence officer, an authorised law enforcement officer or a foreign officer—the name of the officer;  (h) if the authority relates to an authorised civilian whose supervisor is a law enforcement officer:  (i) the name of the authorised civilian; and  (ii) the name of his or her supervisor under the authority; and  (iii) the period for which the authority will remain in force, being a period not exceeding 3 months;  (i) if the authority relates to an authorised civilian whose supervisor is an intelligence officer: ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and witness identity protection  Schedule 3 Main amendments  Part 1  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010  (i) the name of the authorised civilian; and  (ii) the name of his or her supervisor under the authority."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "66b6e08807ae8e6e917b1674186e3d371a5184142984d0fc97c77e289464f041" ;
    values:partOf concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15kc ;
    cof:pageNumber "120"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Authority must state certain details" ;
    dc:description "Details of assumed identity, evidence, conditions, and officer names" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
