doc:sch-3-sec-15kc-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "15KC(2) Form of authority" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) An authority must state the following:  (a) the name of the person granting the authority;  (b) the date of the authority;  (c) details of the assumed identity authorised;  (d) details of any evidence of the assumed identity that may be acquired under the authority;  (e) the conditions (if any) to which the authority is subject;  (f) why the authority is granted;  (g) if the authority relates to an authorised intelligence officer, an authorised law enforcement officer or a foreign officer—the name of the officer;  (h) if the authority relates to an authorised civilian whose supervisor is a law enforcement officer:  (i) the name of the authorised civilian; and  (ii) the name of his or her supervisor under the authority; and  (iii) the period for which the authority will remain in force, being a period not exceeding 3 months;  (i) if the authority relates to an authorised civilian whose supervisor is an intelligence officer: ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and witness identity protection  Schedule 3 Main amendments  Part 1  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010  (i) the name of the authorised civilian; and  (ii) the name of his or her supervisor under the authority." ;
    cof:pageNumber "120"^^xsd:integer .

concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15kc-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "15KC(3) Form of authority"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-15kc-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) The authority must also state the following:  (a) each issuing agency to which a request may be made under section 15KI or 15KX;  (b) whether it authorises an application under a corresponding assumed identity law for an order for an entry in a register of births, deaths or marriages;  (c) whether the assumed identity can be used in a foreign country and the reasons for the need for this use. Note: The chief officer may delegate functions under this section—see section 15LH." ;
    skos:definition "(3) The authority must also state the following:  (a) each issuing agency to which a request may be made under section 15KI or 15KX;  (b) whether it authorises an application under a corresponding assumed identity law for an order for an entry in a register of births, deaths or marriages;  (c) whether the assumed identity can be used in a foreign country and the reasons for the need for this use. Note: The chief officer may delegate functions under this section—see section 15LH."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "e06d7269e22f53f0abf1635dd6bb1f96b9454735f4baf279670c2036701bd257" ;
    values:partOf concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15kc ;
    cof:pageNumber "120"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Must state issuing agencies and conditions for assumed identity use." ;
    dc:description "Yes" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
