concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15kp a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "15KP Assumed identity may be acquired and used"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-15kp ;
    values:originalText "A person may acquire or use an assumed identity if:  (a) the person is an authorised person (other than an authorised civilian) and the acquisition or use is:  (i) in accordance with an authority; and  (ii) in the course of duty; or  (b) the person is an authorised civilian and the acquisition or use is in accordance with:  (i) an authority; and  (ii) any direction by the person’s supervisor under the authority. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and witness identity protection  Schedule 3 Main amendments  Part 1  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010" ;
    skos:definition "A person may acquire or use an assumed identity if:  (a) the person is an authorised person (other than an authorised civilian) and the acquisition or use is:  (i) in accordance with an authority; and  (ii) in the course of duty; or  (b) the person is an authorised civilian and the acquisition or use is in accordance with:  (i) an authority; and  (ii) any direction by the person’s supervisor under the authority. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and witness identity protection  Schedule 3 Main amendments  Part 1  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "86bd2912ff8597341f2399c3f6f3cfc5c3351d13fc86d6081abd5e4ca46e5ee5" ;
    cof:pageNumber "126"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Acquiring or using an assumed identity is permitted under certain conditions." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
