concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15kt a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "15KT Particular qualifications"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-15kt ;
    values:originalText "(1) Sections 15KQ, 15KR and 15KS do not apply to anything done by an authorised person if:  (a) a particular qualification is needed to do the thing; and  (b) the person does not have that qualification.  (2) Subsection (1) applies whether or not the person has acquired, as evidence of an assumed identity, a document that indicates that he or she has that qualification. Example: An officer who cannot fly a plane is not authorised to fly even though he or she has acquired a pilot’s licence under an assumed identity." ;
    skos:definition "(1) Sections 15KQ, 15KR and 15KS do not apply to anything done by an authorised person if:  (a) a particular qualification is needed to do the thing; and  (b) the person does not have that qualification.  (2) Subsection (1) applies whether or not the person has acquired, as evidence of an assumed identity, a document that indicates that he or she has that qualification. Example: An officer who cannot fly a plane is not authorised to fly even though he or she has acquired a pilot’s licence under an assumed identity."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "0f5effcefb191742d1ae2eba542a0a965f017d1d23b18caacf0ca2090b9b8b9b" ;
    cof:pageNumber "128"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15kt-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15kt-ss-2 ;
