doc:sch-3-sec-15kx-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "15KX(2) Requests to a participating jurisdiction for evidence of" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) The chief officer of a law enforcement agency or an intelligence agency who grants the authority may request the chief officer of an issuing agency of a participating jurisdiction stated in the authority to:  (a) produce evidence of the assumed identity in accordance with the authority; and  (b) give evidence of the assumed identity to the following:  (i) the authorised person named in the authority;  (ii) an officer of the law enforcement agency or the intelligence agency who is named in the request. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115  Schedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and witness identity protection" ;
    cof:pageNumber "131"^^xsd:integer .

concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-128 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "128 Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-128 ;
    values:originalText "Note 1: The chief officer may delegate functions under this section—see section 15LH. Note 2: Section 15KW modifies the effect of this provision if control of the authority is transferred.  (3) The request must state that it is a request under this section.  (4) A request must not be made under this section for an entry in a register of births, deaths or marriages." ;
    skos:definition "Note 1: The chief officer may delegate functions under this section—see section 15LH. Note 2: Section 15KW modifies the effect of this provision if control of the authority is transferred.  (3) The request must state that it is a request under this section.  (4) A request must not be made under this section for an entry in a register of births, deaths or marriages."@en ;
