    skos:definition "(3) if the person causes the disclosure of information mentioned in paragraph (1)(c), (2)(c) or (3)(c) (as the case may be) and the disclosure is:  (a) in connection with the administration or execution of this Part or a corresponding assumed identity law; or  (b) for the purposes of any legal proceeding arising out of or otherwise related to this Part or a corresponding assumed identity law or of any report of any such proceedings; or  (c) made by the Commonwealth Director of Public Prosecutions for the purposes of a legal proceeding; or ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115  Schedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and witness identity protection"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "e9892bfc0c2f8236763289c2224977e26c9f417f46159411b9c4fe2239f67dec" ;
    values:partOf concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15lc ;
    cof:pageNumber "134"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Disclosing information about assumed identity is prohibited unless specified conditions are met. Disclosing information about assumed identity is an offence." ;
