doc:sch-3-sec-15ld-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "15LD(2) Reports about authorities for assumed identities etc.—law" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) The chief officer must advise the Minister of any information in the report that, in the chief officer’s opinion, should be excluded from the report before the report is laid before the Parliament ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and witness identity protection  Schedule 3 Main amendments  Part 1  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010 because the information, if made public, could reasonably be expected to:  (a) endanger a person’s safety; or  (b) prejudice an investigation or prosecution; or  (c) compromise any law enforcement agency’s operational activities or methodologies." ;
    cof:pageNumber "136"^^xsd:integer .

concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15ld-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "15LD(3) Reports about authorities for assumed identities etc.—law"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-15ld-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) The Minister must exclude information from the report if satisfied on the advice of the chief officer of any of the grounds set out in subsection (2) and must cause a copy of the report to be laid before each House of the Parliament within 15 sitting days of that House after the day on which the Minister receives the report." ;
    skos:definition "(3) The Minister must exclude information from the report if satisfied on the advice of the chief officer of any of the grounds set out in subsection (2) and must cause a copy of the report to be laid before each House of the Parliament within 15 sitting days of that House after the day on which the Minister receives the report."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "6d4a12d54dc02b73433f33d50b0aa41aafb611ec7196a4fe189a4e16d7b46db0" ;
