concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15le a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "15LE Reports about authorities for assumed identities etc.—"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-15le ;
    values:originalText "intelligence agencies  As soon as practicable after the end of each financial year, the chief officer of an intelligence agency must submit a report to the Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security (the Inspector-General) that includes the following information for the year:  (a) the number of authorities granted during the year;  (b) a general description of the activities undertaken by authorised civilians and authorised intelligence officers when using assumed identities under this Part during the year;  (c) the number of applications for authorities that were refused during the year;  (d) the number of authorities of which control was transferred by the chief officer under section 15KV during the year;  (e) the number of authorities of which control was transferred to the chief officer under section 15KV during the year;  (f) a statement whether or not any fraud or other unlawful activity was identified by an audit under section 15LG during the year;  (g) any other information relating to authorities and assumed identities and the administration of this Part that the Inspector-General considers appropriate. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115  Schedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and witness identity protection" ;
    skos:definition "intelligence agencies  As soon as practicable after the end of each financial year, the chief officer of an intelligence agency must submit a report to the Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security (the Inspector-General) that includes the following information for the year:  (a) the number of authorities granted during the year;  (b) a general description of the activities undertaken by authorised civilians and authorised intelligence officers when using assumed identities under this Part during the year;  (c) the number of applications for authorities that were refused during the year;  (d) the number of authorities of which control was transferred by the chief officer under section 15KV during the year;  (e) the number of authorities of which control was transferred to the chief officer under section 15KV during the year;  (f) a statement whether or not any fraud or other unlawful activity was identified by an audit under section 15LG during the year;  (g) any other information relating to authorities and assumed identities and the administration of this Part that the Inspector-General considers appropriate. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115  Schedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and witness identity protection"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "b4ccab7d34d97f725e75552636be04c808fe8ff4ccc000eec3f0ba2c8bab9729" ;
    cof:pageNumber "137"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Chief officer of an intelligence agency must submit a report to the Inspector-General." ;
    dc:description "Yes" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf> ;
