doc:sch-3-sec-15mp-ss-4 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "15MP(4) Appeals and adjournments" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(4) If a party to the proceedings appeals against the decision to give or refuse leave, or to make or refuse to make the order, the appeal court may allow the operative to whom the certificate relates, or the chief officer who gave the certificate, to join the appeal as a respondent, if the appeal court is satisfied that the operative or chief officer has a sufficient interest in the decision." ;
    cof:pageNumber "154"^^xsd:integer .

concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15mp-ss-5 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "15MP(5) Appeals and adjournments"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-15mp-ss-5 ;
    values:originalText "(5) A party to the proceedings, the operative to whom the certificate relates or the chief officer who gave the certificate may apply to the original court for an adjournment:  (a) to appeal against the decision of the original court to give or refuse leave, or to make or refuse to make the order; or  (b) to decide whether to appeal or seek leave to appeal against the decision." ;
    skos:definition "(5) A party to the proceedings, the operative to whom the certificate relates or the chief officer who gave the certificate may apply to the original court for an adjournment:  (a) to appeal against the decision of the original court to give or refuse leave, or to make or refuse to make the order; or  (b) to decide whether to appeal or seek leave to appeal against the decision."@en ;
