concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15ms a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "15MS Disclosure offences"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-15ms ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person commits an offence if:  (a) a witness identity protection certificate for an operative in relation to a proceeding has been given; and  (b) the certificate has not been cancelled under section 15MQ; and  (c) the person engages in conduct; and  (d) the conduct results in the disclosure of the operative’s identity or where the operative lives; and  (e) none of the following applies:  (i) the conduct is required by section 15ML;  (ii) the conduct is authorised by leave or by an order under section 15MM;  (iii) the conduct is permitted under section 15MR. Penalty: Imprisonment for 2 years.  (2) A person commits an offence if: ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and witness identity protection  Schedule 3 Main amendments  Part 1  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010  (a) a witness identity protection certificate for an operative in relation to a proceeding has been given; and  (b) the certificate has not been cancelled under section 15MQ; and  (c) the person engages in conduct; and  (d) the conduct results in the disclosure of the operative’s identity or where the operative lives; and  (e) none of the following applies:  (i) the conduct is required by section 15ML;  (ii) the conduct is authorised by leave or by an order under section 15MM;  (iii) the conduct is permitted under section 15MR; and  (f) the person is reckless as to whether his or her conduct will endanger the health or safety of another person. Penalty: Imprisonment for 10 years.  (3) A person commits an offence if:  (a) a witness identity protection certificate for an operative in relation to a proceeding has been given; and  (b) the certificate has not been cancelled under section 15MQ; and  (c) the person engages in conduct; and  (d) the conduct results in the disclosure of the operative’s identity or where the operative lives; and  (e) none of the following applies:  (i) the conduct is required by section 15ML;  (ii) the conduct is authorised by leave or by an order under section 15MM;  (iii) the conduct is permitted under section 15MR; and  (f) the person is reckless as to whether his or her conduct will:  (i) prejudice any current or future investigation; or  (ii) prejudice any current or future activity relating to security. Penalty: Imprisonment for 10 years. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115  Schedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and witness identity protection" ;
    skos:definition "(1) A person commits an offence if:  (a) a witness identity protection certificate for an operative in relation to a proceeding has been given; and  (b) the certificate has not been cancelled under section 15MQ; and  (c) the person engages in conduct; and  (d) the conduct results in the disclosure of the operative’s identity or where the operative lives; and  (e) none of the following applies:  (i) the conduct is required by section 15ML;  (ii) the conduct is authorised by leave or by an order under section 15MM;  (iii) the conduct is permitted under section 15MR. Penalty: Imprisonment for 2 years.  (2) A person commits an offence if: ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and witness identity protection  Schedule 3 Main amendments  Part 1  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010  (a) a witness identity protection certificate for an operative in relation to a proceeding has been given; and  (b) the certificate has not been cancelled under section 15MQ; and  (c) the person engages in conduct; and  (d) the conduct results in the disclosure of the operative’s identity or where the operative lives; and  (e) none of the following applies:  (i) the conduct is required by section 15ML;  (ii) the conduct is authorised by leave or by an order under section 15MM;  (iii) the conduct is permitted under section 15MR; and  (f) the person is reckless as to whether his or her conduct will endanger the health or safety of another person. Penalty: Imprisonment for 10 years.  (3) A person commits an offence if:  (a) a witness identity protection certificate for an operative in relation to a proceeding has been given; and  (b) the certificate has not been cancelled under section 15MQ; and  (c) the person engages in conduct; and  (d) the conduct results in the disclosure of the operative’s identity or where the operative lives; and  (e) none of the following applies:  (i) the conduct is required"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "c5405c886aec1b0288b47cbc53feb3c3253d409fbb9c3f2651c2c1223def4f61" ;
    cof:pageNumber "156"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15ms-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15ms-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15ms-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf> ;
    dc:source "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.156" .
