doc:sch-3-sec-15ms-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "15MS(1) Disclosure offences" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person commits an offence if:  (a) a witness identity protection certificate for an operative in relation to a proceeding has been given; and  (b) the certificate has not been cancelled under section 15MQ; and  (c) the person engages in conduct; and  (d) the conduct results in the disclosure of the operative’s identity or where the operative lives; and  (e) none of the following applies:  (i) the conduct is required by section 15ML;  (ii) the conduct is authorised by leave or by an order under section 15MM;  (iii) the conduct is permitted under section 15MR. Penalty: Imprisonment for 2 years." ;
    cof:pageNumber "156"^^xsd:integer .

concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15ms-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "15MS(2) Disclosure offences"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-15ms-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) A person commits an offence if: ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and witness identity protection  Schedule 3 Main amendments  Part 1  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010  (a) a witness identity protection certificate for an operative in relation to a proceeding has been given; and  (b) the certificate has not been cancelled under section 15MQ; and  (c) the person engages in conduct; and  (d) the conduct results in the disclosure of the operative’s identity or where the operative lives; and  (e) none of the following applies:  (i) the conduct is required by section 15ML;  (ii) the conduct is authorised by leave or by an order under section 15MM;  (iii) the conduct is permitted under section 15MR; and  (f) the person is reckless as to whether his or her conduct will endanger the health or safety of another person. Penalty: Imprisonment for 10 years." ;
    skos:definition "(2) A person commits an offence if: ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and witness identity protection  Schedule 3 Main amendments  Part 1  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010  (a) a witness identity protection certificate for an operative in relation to a proceeding has been given; and  (b) the certificate has not been cancelled under section 15MQ; and  (c) the person engages in conduct; and  (d) the conduct results in the disclosure of the operative’s identity or where the operative lives; and  (e) none of the following applies:  (i) the conduct is required by section 15ML;  (ii) the conduct is authorised by leave or by an order under section 15MM;  (iii) the conduct is permitted under section 15MR; and  (f) the person is reckless as to whether his or her conduct will endanger the health or safety of another person. Penalty: Imprisonment for 10 years."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "bff9adf1a1e8b861414001cc642653b9fe787a583b57841fab239fc067751f22" ;
    values:partOf concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15ms ;
    cof:pageNumber "156"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Disclosure of operative's identity or where the operative lives is prohibited." ;
