concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-16 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "16 Definitions"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-16 ;
    values:originalText "In this Part: commencement means the commencement of this item. State controlled operations law means:  (a) a law of a State or Territory; or  (b) a provision or provisions of a law of a State or Territory; prescribed by the regulations for the purposes of this definition. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115  Schedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and witness identity protection" ;
    skos:definition "In this Part: commencement means the commencement of this item. State controlled operations law means:  (a) a law of a State or Territory; or  (b) a provision or provisions of a law of a State or Territory; prescribed by the regulations for the purposes of this definition. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115  Schedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and witness identity protection"@en ;
