concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-17 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "17 Controlled operations authorised before commencement"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-17 ;
    values:originalText "continue under old law (1) Despite the repeals and amendments made by this Part, the Crimes Act 1914, as in force immediately before the commencement of this item, continues to apply after that commencement, in relation to a pre-commencement controlled operation, as if those repeals and amendments had not happened. (2) In this item: pre-commencement controlled operation means a controlled operation authorised under Part IAB of the Crimes Act 1914 before the commencement of this item, whether or not the pre-commencement controlled operation had been completed as at that commencement." ;
    skos:definition "continue under old law (1) Despite the repeals and amendments made by this Part, the Crimes Act 1914, as in force immediately before the commencement of this item, continues to apply after that commencement, in relation to a pre-commencement controlled operation, as if those repeals and amendments had not happened. (2) In this item: pre-commencement controlled operation means a controlled operation authorised under Part IAB of the Crimes Act 1914 before the commencement of this item, whether or not the pre-commencement controlled operation had been completed as at that commencement."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "291cbb5d04c866060db5b55141997d2fd83b9a66fd0abfcb0580caf2d5e39d31" ;
    cof:pageNumber "166"^^xsd:integer ;
