doc:sch-3-sec-19 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "19 Assumed identities—authorisations taken to be authority" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "under new law (1) This item applies to an authorisation that was granted under section 15XG of the Crimes Act 1914 immediately before the commencement of this item. (2) The authorisation has effect, after the commencement of this item, as if it were an authority granted under section 15KB as inserted by this Schedule." ;
    cof:pageNumber "166"^^xsd:integer .

concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-20 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "20 Assumed identities—continuation of old law in relation to"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-20 ;
    values:originalText "States without corresponding laws (1) Despite the repeal of Part IAC of the Crimes Act 1914 by this Schedule: ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and witness identity protection  Schedule 3 General application and transitional provisions  Part 3  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010  (a) section 15XH of that Act, as in force immediately before the commencement of this item, continues in effect after that commencement, in relation to a State or Territory that is not a participating jurisdiction, as if that repeal had not happened; and  (b) that Part, and any other provision of the Crimes Act 1914 that relates to the operation of that Part, continues in effect in relation to authorisations under that Part and assumed identities acquired or used under such authorisations as if that repeal had not happened. (2) In this item: participating jurisdiction has the same meaning as in section 15K of the Crimes Act 1914, as in force immediately after the commencement of this item. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115  Schedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and witness identity protection" ;
    skos:definition "States without corresponding laws (1) Despite the repeal of Part IAC of the Crimes Act 1914 by this Schedule: ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and witness identity protection  Schedule 3 General application and transitional provisions  Part 3  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010  (a) section 15XH of that Act, as in force immediately before the commencement of this item, continues in effect after that commencement, in relation to a State or Territory that is not a participating jurisdiction, as if that repeal had not happened; and  (b) that Part, and any other provision of the Crimes Act 1914 that relates to the operation of that Part, continues in effect in relation to authorisations under that Part and assumed identities acquired or used under such authorisations as if that repeal had not happened. (2) In this item: participating jurisdiction has the same meaning as in section 15K of the Crimes Act 1914, as in force immediately after the commencement of this item. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115  Schedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and witness identity protection"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "c93952136c0bd313fe4fe8043cb109dda7b43687bb00db6e50d07806682d62a7" ;
    cof:pageNumber "166"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "States without corresponding laws: continuation of old law in relation to" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
