    cof:title "166(4) Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(4) For a person to be guilty of an offence because of the operation of this section, the person and at least one other party to the agreement must have intended that an offence would be committed under the agreement. Agreement may be non-verbal etc." ;
    cof:pageNumber "170"^^xsd:integer .

concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-4-sec-166-ss-5 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "166(5) Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-166-ss-5 ;
    values:originalText "(5) The agreement:  (a) may consist of a non-verbal understanding; and  (b) may be entered into before, or at the same time as, the conduct constituting any of the physical elements of the joint offence was engaged in. Termination of involvement etc." ;
    skos:definition "(5) The agreement:  (a) may consist of a non-verbal understanding; and  (b) may be entered into before, or at the same time as, the conduct constituting any of the physical elements of the joint offence was engaged in. Termination of involvement etc."@en ;
