concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-4-sec-166-ss-6 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "166(6) Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-166-ss-6 ;
    values:originalText "(6) A person cannot be found guilty of an offence because of the operation of this section if, before the conduct constituting any of the physical elements of the joint offence concerned was engaged in, the person: ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115  Other amendments  Schedule 4 Joint commission  Part 1  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010  (a) terminated his or her involvement; and  (b) took all reasonable steps to prevent that conduct from being engaged in. Person may be found guilty even if another party not prosecuted etc." ;
    skos:definition "(6) A person cannot be found guilty of an offence because of the operation of this section if, before the conduct constituting any of the physical elements of the joint offence concerned was engaged in, the person: ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115  Other amendments  Schedule 4 Joint commission  Part 1  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010  (a) terminated his or her involvement; and  (b) took all reasonable steps to prevent that conduct from being engaged in. Person may be found guilty even if another party not prosecuted etc."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "bd17477117562a269bf11bb6929d69992b2a5dad14d76ac79e48681e67dd5da7" ;
    values:partOf concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-4-sec-166 ;
    cof:pageNumber "170"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "A person cannot be found guilty of an offence if they terminated their involvement and took reasonable steps to prevent the conduct." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf> ;
