doc:sch-4-sec-166-ss-6 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "166(6) Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(6) A person cannot be found guilty of an offence because of the operation of this section if, before the conduct constituting any of the physical elements of the joint offence concerned was engaged in, the person: ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115  Other amendments  Schedule 4 Joint commission  Part 1  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010  (a) terminated his or her involvement; and  (b) took all reasonable steps to prevent that conduct from being engaged in. Person may be found guilty even if another party not prosecuted etc." ;
    cof:pageNumber "170"^^xsd:integer .

concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-4-sec-166-ss-7 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "166(7) Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-166-ss-7 ;
    values:originalText "(7) A person may be found guilty of an offence because of the operation of this section even if:  (a) another party to the agreement has not been prosecuted or has not been found guilty; or  (b) the person was not present when any of the conduct constituting the physical elements of the joint offence was engaged in. Special liability provisions apply" ;
    skos:definition "(7) A person may be found guilty of an offence because of the operation of this section even if:  (a) another party to the agreement has not been prosecuted or has not been found guilty; or  (b) the person was not present when any of the conduct constituting the physical elements of the joint offence was engaged in. Special liability provisions apply"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "8338932c98225d5328c437dae73d1f663bfef70ad811a9929c1bc7a2f53550d9" ;
    values:partOf concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-4-sec-166 ;
    cof:pageNumber "170"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "A person may be found guilty of an offence despite another party not being prosecuted or present." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
