concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-4-sec-18j a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "18J Application"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-18j ;
    values:originalText "The Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979, as amended by this Division, applies in relation to the communication, use and making of a record of information, and the giving of information in evidence in proceedings, on or after the commencement of this item, whether the information was obtained before or after that commencement. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115  Other amendments  Schedule 4 Regulations  Part 3  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010" ;
    skos:definition "The Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979, as amended by this Division, applies in relation to the communication, use and making of a record of information, and the giving of information in evidence in proceedings, on or after the commencement of this item, whether the information was obtained before or after that commencement. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115  Other amendments  Schedule 4 Regulations  Part 3  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010"@en ;
